{"id":"mahabharata-13-008","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":8,"title":"अष्टमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 8 · Whom should one honour?","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks whom Bhishma honours and bows to. Bhishma answers that many are heroes in battle but few are givers without envy, and that he honours those whom he wishes to be like, and tells the duty of a king to guard brahmins as a father guards his sons.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಯಾರನ್ನು ಗೌರವಿಸಿ ನಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ವೀರರು ಅನೇಕರು, ಅಸೂಯೆಯಿಲ್ಲದ ದಾನಿಗಳು ವಿರಳ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳಿ ತಂದೆ ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಕಾಯುವಂತೆ ರಾಜ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರನ್ನು ಕಾಯಬೇಕೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि भीष्म किन्हें पूजते और नमन करते हैं। भीष्म कहते हैं कि युद्ध में वीर बहुत हैं पर ईर्ष्यारहित दाता कम, और राजा को ब्राह्मणों की रक्षा पिता की तरह पुत्रों के लिए करनी चाहिए।","te":"భీష్ముడు ఎవరిని గౌరవించి నమస్కరిస్తాడని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. యుద్ధంలో వీరులు చాలామంది, అసూయ లేని దాతలు అరుదని చెప్పి, తండ్రి కొడుకులను కాపాడినట్లు రాజు బ్రాహ్మణులను కాపాడాలని అంటాడు.","ta":"பீஷ்மர் யாரை மதித்து வணங்குகிறார் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, போரில் வீரர் பலர், பொறாமையற்ற கொடையாளிகள் சிலரே என்று கூறி, தந்தை மக்களைக் காப்பது போல் மன்னன் அந்தணரைக் காக்க வேண்டும் என்கிறார்.","ml":"ആരെയാണ് ആദരിക്കുന്നതും വണങ്ങുന്നതും എന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭീഷ്മരോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു. യുദ്ധത്തിൽ വീരന്മാർ പലരുണ്ടെങ്കിലും അസൂയയില്ലാതെ ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നവർ വിരളമാണെന്നും, താൻ ആരെപ്പോലെയാകാൻ ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നുവോ അവരെയാണ് ആദരിക്കുന്നതെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. പിതാവ് പുത്രന്മാരെ കാക്കുന്നതുപോലെ ബ്രാഹ്മണരെ സംരക്ഷിക്കുക എന്നത് രാജാവിന്റെ കടമയാണെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.8; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"के पूज्याः के नमस्कार्याः कान्नमस्यसि भारत ।\nएतन्मे सर्वमाचक्ष्व येषां स्पृहयसे नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whom should one honor, whom bow to, whom do you revere, Bharata? Tell me all this: those you hold dear."}},{"n":2,"text":"उत्तमापद्गतस्यापि यत्र ते वर्तते मनः ।\nमनुष्यलोके सर्वस्मिन्यदमुत्रेह चाप्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me those to whom your mind turns, even in the worst calamity, in all the human world and in the next."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"स्पृहयामि द्विजातीनां येषां ब्रह्म परं धनम् ।\nयेषां स्वप्रत्ययः स्वर्गस्तपःस्वाध्यायसाधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cherish the twice-born for whom Brahman is the highest wealth, whose own conviction is their heaven, and whose means are austerity and Vedic study."}},{"n":4,"text":"येषां वृद्धाश्च बालाश्च पितृपैतामहीं धुरम् ।\nउद्वहन्ति न सीदन्ति तेषां वै स्पृहयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cherish those whose elders and young alike carry the load of their fathers and grandfathers without faltering."}},{"n":5,"text":"विद्यास्वभिविनीतानां दान्तानां मृदुभाषिणाम् ।\nश्रुतवृत्तोपपन्नानां सदाक्षरविदां सताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cherish those who are well trained in the sciences, self-controlled and soft-spoken, endowed with learning and conduct, the good, who always know the imperishable."}},{"n":6,"text":"संसत्सु वदतां येषां हंसानामिव संघशः ।\nमङ्गल्यरूपा रुचिरा दिव्यजीमूतनिःस्वनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their lovely, auspicious voices, deep as divine thunder-clouds, are heard in assemblies like flocks of swans."}},{"n":7,"text":"सम्यगुच्चारिता वाचः श्रूयन्ते हि युधिष्ठिर ।\nशुश्रूषमाणे नृपतौ प्रेत्य चेह सुखावहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Words rightly uttered by them are heard, Yudhishthira; they bring happiness here and hereafter to a king who listens."}},{"n":8,"text":"ये चापि तेषां श्रोतारः सदा सदसि संमताः ।\nविज्ञानगुणसंपन्नास्तेषां च स्पृहयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cherish also their listeners, always honored in assemblies and rich in knowledge and virtue."}},{"n":9,"text":"सुसंस्कृतानि प्रयताः शुचीनि गुणवन्ति च ।\nददत्यन्नानि तृप्त्यर्थं ब्राह्मणेभ्यो युधिष्ठिर ।\nये चापि सततं राजंस्तेषां च स्पृहयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, I cherish too those who, ever disciplined, offer brahmins well-prepared, pure and excellent food for their satisfaction."}},{"n":10,"text":"शक्यं ह्येवाहवे योद्धुं न दातुमनसूयितम् ।\nशूरा वीराश्च शतशः सन्ति लोके युधिष्ठिर ।\nतेषां संख्यायमानानां दानशूरो विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is possible to fight in battle but hard to give without envy. In the world there are heroes and brave men by the hundred; of those counted, the hero of giving stands out."}},{"n":11,"text":"धन्यः स्यां यद्यहं भूयः सौम्य ब्राह्मणकोऽपि वा ।\nकुले जातो धर्मगतिस्तपोविद्यापरायणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gentle one, I would count myself fortunate if I were born again, even as a lowly brahmin, in a family that follows dharma and is devoted to austerity and learning."}},{"n":12,"text":"न मे त्वत्तः प्रियतरो लोकेऽस्मिन्पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nत्वत्तश्च मे प्रियतरा ब्राह्मणा भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Pandu, no one in this world is dearer to me than you, and brahmins are dearer to me than you, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":13,"text":"यथा मम प्रियतरास्त्वत्तो विप्राः कुरूद्वह ।\nतेन सत्येन गच्छेयं लोकान्यत्र स शंतनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the truth that brahmins are dearer to me than you, upholder of the Kurus, may I go to the worlds where Shantanu is."}},{"n":14,"text":"न मे पिता प्रियतरो ब्राह्मणेभ्यस्तथाभवत् ।\nन मे पितुः पिता वापि ये चान्येऽपि सुहृज्जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither my father nor my father's father, nor any other friends, were dearer to me than brahmins."}},{"n":15,"text":"न हि मे वृजिनं किंचिद्विद्यते ब्राह्मणेष्विह ।\nअणु वा यदि वा स्थूलं विदितं साधुकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know of no wrong, small or great, that I have done to brahmins, as the good know."}},{"n":16,"text":"कर्मणा मनसा वापि वाचा वापि परंतप ।\nयन्मे कृतं ब्राह्मणेषु तेनाद्य न तपाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scorcher of foes, whatever I have done toward brahmins in deed, thought or word, I am not tormented by it today."}},{"n":17,"text":"ब्रह्मण्य इति मामाहुस्तया वाचास्मि तोषितः ।\nएतदेव पवित्रेभ्यः सर्वेभ्यः परमं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call me a friend of brahmins, and by that word I am pleased; this is held to be the highest of all purifiers."}},{"n":18,"text":"पश्यामि लोकानमलाञ्छुचीन्ब्राह्मणयायिनः ।\nतेषु मे तात गन्तव्यमह्नाय च चिराय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see spotless, pure worlds for those who go to brahmins; to those I must go, soon and for long."}},{"n":19,"text":"यथा पत्याश्रयो धर्मः स्त्रीणां लोके युधिष्ठिर ।\nस देवः सा गतिर्नान्या क्षत्रियस्य तथा द्विजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the husband is the support of dharma for women in this world, their god and their only refuge, so brahmins are for a Kshatriya."}},{"n":20,"text":"क्षत्रियः शतवर्षी च दशवर्षी च ब्राह्मणः ।\nपितापुत्रौ च विज्ञेयौ तयोर्हि ब्राह्मणः पिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Kshatriya of a hundred years and a brahmin of ten should be seen as father and son, and of the two the brahmin is the father."}},{"n":21,"text":"नारी तु पत्यभावे वै देवरं कुरुते पतिम् ।\nपृथिवी ब्राह्मणालाभे क्षत्रियं कुरुते पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a woman has no husband she takes her husband's brother as husband; when the earth lacks a brahmin, she takes a Kshatriya as lord."}},{"n":22,"text":"पुत्रवच्च ततो रक्ष्या उपास्या गुरुवच्च ते ।\nअग्निवच्चोपचर्या वै ब्राह्मणाः कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"So brahmins should be protected like sons, served like a teacher, and tended like a fire, best of the Kurus."}},{"n":23,"text":"ऋजून्सतः सत्यशीलान्सर्वभूतहिते रतान् ।\nआशीविषानिव क्रुद्धान्द्विजानुपचरेत्सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should always attend upon the twice-born, upright, good, truthful and devoted to the welfare of all beings, though they are like angry venomous snakes."}},{"n":24,"text":"तेजसस्तपसश्चैव नित्यं बिभ्येद्युधिष्ठिर ।\nउभे चैते परित्याज्ये तेजश्चैव तपस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, one should always fear their energy and austerity; both of these, energy and austerity, should be given up."}},{"n":25,"text":"व्यवसायस्तयोः शीघ्रमुभयोरेव विद्यते ।\nहन्युः क्रुद्धा महाराज ब्राह्मणा ये तपस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both of them act swiftly, great king; brahmins who are ascetics, when angry, can kill."}},{"n":26,"text":"भूयः स्यादुभयं दत्तं ब्राह्मणाद्यदकोपनात् ।\nकुर्यादुभयतःशेषं दत्तशेषं न शेषयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is given to a brahmin without provoking him brings more of both; one should keep a remainder on both sides, and not leave only what has been given."}},{"n":27,"text":"दण्डपाणिर्यथा गोषु पालो नित्यं स्थिरो भवेत् ।\nब्राह्मणान्ब्रह्म च तथा क्षत्रियः परिपालयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a herdsman with staff in hand stays ever steady among his cows, so a Kshatriya should protect brahmins and Brahman."}},{"n":28,"text":"पितेव पुत्रान्रक्षेथा ब्राह्मणान्ब्रह्मतेजसः ।\nगृहे चैषामवेक्षेथाः कच्चिदस्तीह जीवनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Protect brahmins who have the splendor of Brahman as a father protects his sons, and look in at their homes to see whether they have a livelihood."}}]}]}